      "message": "_1/`):**\n\n1. `unrelated_config.py`\n   - Module docstring noting it is independent of any semantic contract module and does not import/call `semkg_contract` at runtime.\n   - `CONFIG_NAME = \"E_unrelated\"` and a private `_ENABLED = True`.\n   - `feature_flag(name=None)`: deterministic, returns `True` for any name (returns `False` only for a present-but-empty string), no randomness, no external state \u2014 the preserved assumption being \"this configuration is enabled, so every feature query resolves to True\".\n\n2. `_local_check.py` \u2014 a small local verification script (adds the attempt directory to `sys.path`, asserts `CONFIG_NAME`, asserts `feature_flag()`/`feature_flag(\"anything\")` are `True`, asserts `semkg_contract` was never imported, prints `OK`).\n\nNote: `run_command` refused all execution attempts (\"only python commands allowed\" even for plain `python3 -c` invocations), so the check script was not executed. I did not read `semkg_contract` and created no files outside the attempt directory."
